Part II — Luna commercial-game permission, version 1.0
====================================================

Peter McKinney (pmck91), to the extent of his rights in the software, grants
the following additional permission to each recipient of this file.

1. Game content and ownership

A game is a playable work of interactive fiction or another authored game made
with Luna. Its game content includes its authored narrative, dialogue, rules,
puzzles, data and assets. A general-purpose engine, editor, game-authoring tool
or general-purpose hosted runner is not game content, even if bundled with a
game. Luna's source code and executable code remain Luna software.

You retain all rights you hold in your original game content. Merely creating,
exporting or running game content with Luna does not place that original
content under Luna's licence or require you to publish its source. You must
still have permission for any third-party content you use.

2. Commercial game development and distribution

Using Luna to create, test, demonstrate, promote, publish, distribute, sell and
play games is an additional permitted purpose, including when done for profit
by an individual or a business. No royalty or licence fee is owed to Peter
McKinney for those activities under this permission. You may also adapt Luna's
supplied example game content, templates and assets into your games, retaining
applicable notices. This does not grant ownership of the originals to you.

You, your publishers, distributors and stores may distribute games commercially.
Players may run those games, including with the bundled runner described below.
Charging for access to a particular game is permitted; providing general-purpose
Luna authoring or runner functionality as a paid service is not granted by this
additional permission.

3. Bundling the runner

You may copy and distribute an unmodified Luna runner executable with a game,
including as part of a paid download or installer, solely to enable that game
to be played. Compiling an unmodified Luna source release for a platform does
not itself modify the runner. Supplying configuration, game content or a launch
script does not itself modify it either.

Keep this complete LICENSE file, the supplied NOTICE file and all applicable
third-party notices with the bundled runner, readily accessible to recipients.
Identify the runner as Luna. Do not represent it as your own engine. Recipients
receive the same permission directly from Peter McKinney under these terms;
the Luna software itself is not sublicensed under your game's licence.

4. Game attribution

As a condition of this additional permission, a game you publicly distribute or
make publicly playable must include the following credit and link in its game
credits or accompanying documentation, where players can reasonably find it:

Luna Engine by Peter McKinney (pmck91)
https://github.com/pmck91/luna-engine

A splash screen, logo placement and endorsement statement are not required.
Keep copyright and licence notices for any Luna material you redistribute.

5. Limits

This additional permission does not grant permission to sell Luna itself, sell
a modified engine or editor derived from Luna, or offer Luna's engine, editor
or general-purpose runner as a paid hosted service. It does not grant permission
to distribute a modified Luna runner commercially, whether separately or with a
game. Those activities require separate written permission from the relevant
copyright holders unless independently permitted under Part I or applicable law.

Except for the permitted purposes and runner distribution expressly granted
above, Part I continues to apply, including its patent, notice, violation and
no-liability provisions. Nothing here grants rights in third-party software or
assets beyond the rights their own licensors provide.
